# D5: named graphs with no triple, and graphs named by a blank node
# (https://github.com/danbri/factoidal/issues/855,
# https://github.com/danbri/factoidal/issues/856). RDF 1.1 Concepts section 4:
# a named graph is a graph name (an IRI or a blank node) and an RDF graph, and
# the RDF graph can be empty. Six named graphs: three IRIs (ex:g0 and ex:g2 have
# no triple) and three blank nodes (_:e and the anonymous one have no triple).
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .

ex:s ex:p ex:o .
ex:g0 { }
ex:g1 { ex:a ex:p ex:b . }
GRAPH ex:g2 { }
_:b1 { ex:c ex:p "x" . }
_:e { }
[] { }
ex:g1 { ex:a2 ex:p ex:b2 }
